              "title": "View body and view-returning helpers exceed nesting/expression thresholds",
              "issue": "Multiple view-returning properties and methods exceed the SUI-1 thresholds. `body` (lines 319-343) reaches nesting depth ≥3 (VStack > VStack > HStack > ...) with conditional branches. `logHeader` (260-317) contains 8+ view expressions (HStack, 4× Button, 2× HStack, Image, Text, StatusDot, Spacer, etc.) with depth ≥3. `logContent` (345-429) holds the largest tree — ScrollView > LazyVStack > ForEach with overlay/task modifiers, far exceeding 5 expressions and depth 2. `messageBubble`, `toolCallChip`, `toolExpandedContent`, `editDiffView`, `writeDiffView`, `hookDetailView`, `permissionPrompt`, `askUserQuestionPrompt`, `planApprovalPrompt`, `inputField`, `taskPanelView`, `mcpDetailView`, and `todoChecklist` each individually breach the threshold (≥5 expressions and/or nesting ≥2). Each should be split into smaller, named subviews — extracting helpers within the same struct does not satisfy SUI-1, since each view-returning property is measured independently.",
              "impact": "The view is hard to read, hard to diff, and hard to test. Diagnostics from the SwiftUI compiler degrade rapidly past these thresholds (\"unable to type-check this expression in reasonable time\").",
              "rule_source": "SUI-1 Body Complexity"
            },
            {
              "id": "sui-004",
