              "title": "View struct contains TRANSFORM logic (collection sort/filter/split) that belongs in the VM",
              "issue": "Four view-struct members perform collection transformation rather than purely declaring UI: (1) `editDiffView` (lines 710-767) splits oldString/newString with `components(separatedBy:)` and branches on line counts; (2) `writeDiffView` (lines 871-909) likewise splits content into lines and branches on counts; (3) `mcpDetailView` (lines 769-795) sorts/maps/joins `d.input` dictionary entries inline; (4) `taskPanelView` (lines 1212-1263) computes `tasks.filter { $0.status == \"completed\" }.count` for the progress badge. Pre-splitting line arrays and pre-computed completion counts should be exposed by `LogViewerViewModel` (or a dedicated formatter) so the View only renders state.",
              "impact": "Mixes data transformation with view declaration — re-runs every body re-evaluation, defeats the View-as-pure-function model, and complicates testability (transform logic cannot be unit-tested without instantiating SwiftUI hosting).",
